            <ArticleTitle>Copper(I)-Catalyzed Ligand-Promoted Multicomponent Reactions of Isocyanides, Selenium, Amines, and Iodoarenes: Access to Highly Functionalized Carbamimidoselenoates.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10866-10874</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.7b01663</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new and facile approach toward highly functionalized carbamimidoseleknoates was developed through the copper(I)-catalyzed ligand-promoted four-component reaction of isocyanides, selenium, amines, and aryl iodides. The reaction constructed a range of organoselenium compounds containing an isoselenourea skeleton with potential bioactivity directly from selenium powder. The simplicity of method and broad diversity of substrates also highlight this work.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
